<!--
doc/src/sgml/ref/listagg.sgml
IvorySQL documentation: Oracle-compatible LISTAGG aggregate
-->

<refentry id="functions-listagg">
 <indexterm zone="functions-listagg">
  <primary>LISTAGG</primary>
 </indexterm>

 <refmeta>
  <refentrytitle>LISTAGG</refentrytitle>
  <manvolnum>7</manvolnum>
  <refmiscinfo>SQL - Language Statements</refmiscinfo>
 </refmeta>

 <refnamediv>
  <refname>LISTAGG</refname>
  <refpurpose>Oracle-compatible ordered string aggregation</refpurpose>
 </refnamediv>

 <refsynopsisdiv>
<synopsis>
LISTAGG( measure_expr [, delimiter ] ) WITHIN GROUP ( ORDER BY sort_expr [, ...] )
</synopsis>
 </refsynopsisdiv>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Description</title>
  <para>
   LISTAGG concatenates values from multiple rows into a single string,
   ordered by the specified sort expression. It is the Oracle-compatible
   equivalent of string_agg with WITHIN GROUP ordering syntax.
  </para>
  <para>
   NULL measure values are ignored. If all values are NULL or the result
   set is empty, LISTAGG returns NULL.
  </para>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Parameters</title>
  <variablelist>
   <varlistentry>
    <term>measure_expr</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      The expression whose values are concatenated. Typically a column
      of type text, varchar2, or any type castable to text.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
   <varlistentry>
    <term>delimiter</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Optional string literal inserted between concatenated values.
      Defaults to empty string if omitted.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
   <varlistentry>
    <term>sort_expr</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      One or more expressions that determine the order of concatenation.
      Multiple columns may be specified comma-separated.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Examples</title>
  <para>Basic ordered concatenation:</para>
<programlisting>
SELECT LISTAGG(ename, ',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY ename)
FROM emp WHERE deptno = 10;
-- Result: CLARK,KING,MILLER
</programlisting>
  <para>Grouped aggregation:</para>
<programlisting>
SELECT deptno, LISTAGG(ename, ' | ') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY sal DESC)
FROM emp GROUP BY deptno;
</programlisting>
  <para>Single-argument form (no delimiter):</para>
<programlisting>
SELECT LISTAGG(ename) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY ename) FROM emp;
</programlisting>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Implementation Notes</title>
  <para>
   Internally, LISTAGG is implemented as a syntax transformation to
   string_agg with an ORDER BY clause. The sys.ora_listagg_check
   function validates the result. The STRAGG function in the sys schema
   provides a simpler comma-delimited alternative without WITHIN GROUP.
  </para>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Compatibility</title>
  <para>
   LISTAGG with WITHIN GROUP is an Oracle Database extension.
   Standard PostgreSQL uses string_agg(expr, delimiter ORDER BY ...).
   IvorySQL supports both syntaxes in Oracle-compatible mode.
  </para>
 </refsect1>
</refentry>
